  "summary_en": "UK Act regulating self-driving road vehicles in Great Britain. It creates a pre-market authorisation regime with an authorised self-driving entity, operator licensing for no-user-in-charge journeys, user-in-charge immunity, new offences, incident investigators, marketing restrictions, passenger service permits, and enforcement powers. Commencement is staged; this version reflects the 2026 position.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Secretary of State authorises vehicles meeting the self-driving test, assessed against a statement of safety principles (at least as safe as careful, competent drivers).",
   "Authorised self-driving entity bears responsibility for the vehicle; no-user-in-charge operators must be licensed.",
   "User-in-charge is immune from liability for the driving of the vehicle, with defined exceptions.",
   "Information offences, civil sanctions (compliance, redress, monetary penalties), and statutory incident inspectors.",
   "Restrictions on misleading self-driving marketing terms, and permits for automated passenger services."
  ],
